# Fixtures

```rocci
@fixture{target: TodoItem}
todoItemExample = { item: { id: 1, text: "Buy milk" } }
```

The marker is stripped; the binding stays ordinary Roc. `target` is a local
PascalCase component or a module-qualified path. Unqualified targets must name
a `@component` in the same file. Dotted targets are left to Roc.

`rocci view` and `rocci browse` consume fixtures. `rocci view` ignores HTTP
declarations. `@test{fixture: name}` pairs a test with a fixture binding.

**Errors:** `@fixture` inside a component body; missing local target.

**Related:** [Tests](/docs/reference/language/tests/),
[CLI view](/docs/reference/cli/#view).
